 C, Delworth T, et al. (2007) The WCRP \nCMIP3 multimodel dataset—a new era in climate change research. Bull Am Meteorol Soc 88:1383–1394.\nMiao Y, Zhou ZX, Jiang MG, et al. (2022) Resistance and \nresilience of nine plant species to drought in Inner Mongolia temperate grasslands of northern China. Appl Sci  \n12:4967.\nMueller KE, Ocheltree TW, Kray JA, et al. (2022) Trading \nwater for carbon in the future: effects of elevated CO\n2 and \nwarming on leaf hydraulic traits in a semiarid grassland. Glob Change Biol 28:5991–6001.\nOrt DR, Baker NR (2002) A photoprotective role for O\n2 as an \nalternative electron sink in photosynthesis? Curr Opin Plant \nBiol 5:193–198.\nSmith MD (2011) The ecological role of climate extremes: \ncurrent understanding and future prospects. J Ecol \n99:651–655.\nSmith MD, Knapp AK, Collins SL (2009) A framework for \nassessing ecosystem dynamics in response to chronic \nresource alterations induced by global change. Ecology 90:3279–3289.\nSpinoni J, Vogt JV, Naumann G, et al. (2018) Will drought \nevents become more frequent and severe in Europe? Int J \nClimatol 38:1718–1736.\nStuart-Haëntjens E, De Boeck HJ, Lemoine NP, et al. (2018) \nMean annual precipitation predicts primary production resistance and resilience to extreme drought. Sci Total \nEnviron 636:360–366.\nSun JM, Zhang B, Pan QM, et al. (2023) Non-linear response \nof productivity to precipitation extremes in the Inner \nMongolia grassland. Funct Ecol 37:1663–1673.\nTielbörger K, Bilton MC, Metz J, et al. (2014) Middle-eastern \nplant communities tolerate 9 years of drought in a multi-\nsite climate manipulation experiment. Nat Commun 5:5102.\nTor-ngern P, Chart-asa C, Chanthorn W, et al. (2021) Variation \nof leaf-level gas exchange rates and leaf functional traits of dominant trees across three successional stages in a Southeast Asian tropical forest. For Ecol Manage 489:119101.\nVitale L, Di Tommasi P, Arena C, et al. (2009) Growth and gas \nexchange response to water shortage of a maize crop on different soil types. Acta Physiol Plant 31:331–341.\nWahab A, Abdi G, Saleem MH, et al. (2022) Plants’ physio-\nbiochemical and phyto-hormonal responses to alleviate the adverse effects of drought stress: a comprehensive review. Plants (Basel) 11:1620.\nWang C, Vera-Vélez R, Lamb EG, et al. (2022) Global pattern \nand associated drivers of grassland productivity sensitivity \nto precipitation change. Sci Total Environ 806:151224.\nWang JF, Zhang LH, Xu XX, et al. (2023) Extreme drought \nalters plant community structure by changing dominant \nspecies growth in desert grassland. J Veg Sci\n 34:e13189.\nWei XN, He W, Zhou YL, et al. (2022) Global assessment of \nlagged and cumulative effects of drought on grassland gross primary production. Ecol Indic 136:108646.\nXu C, Ke YG, Wu HH, et al. (2021) Herbivores alleviate the \nnegative effects of extreme drought on plant community by enhancing dominant species. J. Plant Ecol  14:1030–1036.\nYahdjian L, Sala OE (2002) A rainout shelter design for \nintercepting different amounts of rainfall. Oecologia \n133:95–101.\nYahdjian L, Sala OE, Piñeiro-Guerra JM, et al. (2021) Why \ncoordinated distributed experiments should go global. BioScience 71:918–927.Downloaded from https://academic.oup.com/jpe/article/17/3/rtae027/7642563 by guest on 21 January 2026\n\nCopyedited by: DS11 JOURNAL OF PLANT ECOLOGY | 2024, 17:rtae027Yang W-q, Gu M-y, Kou J-c (2013) Effects of drought \nand rewatering on the photosynthesis and chlorophyll \nfluorescence of Coronilla varia. Acta Agrestia Sin  21:1130–1135.\nYang D, Wang YSD, Wang Q, et al. (2023) Physiological \nresponse and photosynthetic recovery to an extreme drought: evidence from plants in a dry-hot valley savanna of southwest China. Sci Total Environ 868:161711.\nZhang Y, Zhu ZC, Liu Z, et al. (2016) Seasonal and interannual \nchanges in vegetation activity of tropical forests in Southeast Asia. Agric For Meteorol 224:1–10.Downloaded from https://academic.ou