 2019. Benchmarking transposable element an-notation methods for creation of a streamlined, comprehensive pipe-line. Genome Biol 20:275. doi:10.1186/s13059-019-1905-y\nPortugez S, Martin WF, Hazkani-Covo E. 2018. Mosaic mitochondrial-plas-\ntid insertions into the nuclear genome show evidence of both non-ho-mologous end joining and homologous recombination. BMC Evol Biol\n18:162. doi:10.1186/s12862-018-1279-x\nPuertas MJ, González-Sánchez M. 2020. Insertions of mitochondrial DNA\ninto the nucleus —effects and role in cell evolution. Genome 63:365–\n374. doi:10.1139/gen-2019-0151\nQin P, Lu H, Du H, Wang H, Chen W, Chen Z, He Q, Ou S, Zhang H, Li X,\net al. 2021. Pan-genome analysis of 33 genetically diverse rice accessionsGong et al.\n14 Genome Research\nwww.genome.org Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory Press  on June 1, 2025 - Published by genome.cshlp.org Downloaded from \nreveals hidden genomic variations. Cell184: 3542 –3558.e16. doi:10\n.1016/j.cell.2021.04.046\nQuinlan AR, Hall IM. 2010. BEDTools: a flexible suite of utilities for compar-\ning genomic features. Bioinformatics 26:841–842. doi:10.1093/bioinfor\nmatics/btq033\nR Core Team. 2023. R: a language and environment for statistical computing .R\nFoundation for Statistical Computing, Vienna. https://www.R-project\n.org/.\nRicchetti M, Fairhead C, Dujon B. 1999. Mitochondrial DNA repairs double-\nstrand breaks in yeast chromosomes. Nature 402: 96–100. doi:10.1038/\n47076\nRichly E. 2004. NUMTs in sequenced eukaryotic genomes. Mol Biol Evol 21:\n1081 –1084. doi:10.1093/molbev/msh110\nRichly E, Leister D. 2004. NUPTs in sequenced eukaryotes and their geno-\nmic organization in relation to NUMTs. Mol Biol Evol 21:1972 –1980.\ndoi:10.1093/molbev/msh210\nRousseau-Gueutin M, Huang X, Higginson E, Ayliffe M, Day A, Timmis JN.\n2013. Potential functional replacement of the plastidic acetyl-CoA car-boxylase subunit ( accD ) gene by recent transfers to the nucleus in\nsome angiosperm lineages. Plant Physiol 161: 1918 –19