of the AS provides the possibility of abstraction. This is defined as annotation to a parent node when several child nodes are present in the GO candidate collection. This term multiplies the number of total GOs unified at the node by a user defined GO weight factor that controls the possibility and strength of abstraction. c. Finally, the AR selects the lowestterm per branch that lies over a user defined threshold. \nConesa, et al., 2005\n2.4 基因组功能注释\nInterProScan (Jones, et al., 2014)InterProScanis a tool that combines different protein signature recognition methods from the InterPro.https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/\n2.4 基因组功能注释\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/\n\n2.4 基因组功能注释\n\n2.4 基因组功能注释\nInterPro108.0•29th January 2026\n\n2.4 基因组功能注释\neggNOGGene Ontology , KEGG pathways , SMART/PFAM domains  and expanded to CAZyand KEGG modules. \nDavis et al. Genome Biol22, 37 (2021)\n2.5 基因功能富集分析\nRivals, et al., 2007\n2.6 比较基因组\ S. NucleicAcidsRes. 2017 Jan 4;45(D1):D446-D456.GCTATTTTGTCGCTCTC\n\n2.6 比较基因组\nhttps://gold.jgi.doe.gov\n\n2.6 比较基因组\n•基因组家族分析•基于基因的比较•基于序列的比较\n2.6 比较基因组-基于基因\n基因家族的分析\n\n2.6 比较基因组-基于基因\n基因家族的分析\n\n2.6 比较基因组-基于基因\n基于基因的共线性分析\n\n2.6 比较基因组-基于基因\n基于基因的共线性分析\n\n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\n基于序列的共线性分析—syri\n\n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\n基于序列的共线性分析—syri\n\n2.6 比较基因组—基于序列\n•Multi-sequence alignments of large genomic regions are at the core of many computational genome-annotation approaches aimed at identifying coding regions, RNA genes, regulatory regions, and other functional features.\n2.6 比较基因组—基于序列\nWhole-genome alignment•Molecular sequence comparison is one of the most basic and fundamental problems in computational biology•Molecular sequence comparison has been widely used to study the evolutionof whole-genome sequences and gene regulatory regions, gene function prediction, sequence assembly, and relationships among microbial communities. \n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\nMethods•There are two common strategies to tackle the whole-genome alignment problem. •Alignment-based: basing on finding pairwise local alignments and then extending them into multiple local alignments. •Alignment-free (Ren, et al., 2018))\n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\nAlignment-based 1) Local pair-wise alignments are explored only if they contain some type of highly conserved short match, such as balstz, lastz, MUMmerand etc.;2) Once a good seed alignment is found, it is extended to the left and the right using various variants on the Smith-Waterman dynamic programming algorithm, this time allowing for gaps to be inserted. Note that at this stage the arrangement and orientation of pair-wise local alignments are unrestricted and one region can align to more than one other region 3)Sets of pair-wise local alignments can be chained together into sets of colinearregions, using programs like Chaining/Netting.4) Such approaches are inapplicable for unassembled genomes.Blanchette, 2007\n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\nBlanchette, 2007Alignment-based \n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\nAlignment-free§Cactus Comparative power of 240 species (A comparative genomics multitoolfor scientific discovery and conservation, 2020, natural )\n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\nEarl, et al., 201412个比对方法比较\n2.6比较基因组—基于序列\nEarl, et al., 2014评估常用的计算量：Accuracy=(TP+TN)/(FP+FP+TN+FN)Precision=TP/(TP+FP)  (my)Recall=TP/(TP+FN)  (golden)F-score=2*((precision*recall)/(precision+recall))\n(1)Ideally, a genome draft would represent the complete nucleotide base sequence for all chromosomes in the species of interest.(2)There is not one true sequence for a species because of individual genomic variation.(3)Cells from the same individual can differ in genomic content due to somatic mutations. (4)Only a single individual is, but sometimes the genome represents a ‘consensus’ of a number of pooled samples.(5)it is essentially impossible to sequence and assemble all nucleotides in the genome.(6)There will always be some degree of error in the characterized genome sequence, both on the level of individual nucleotides and in the ordering of sequence.EkblomR, Wolf J B W. Evolutionary Applications, 2014, 7(9):1026-1042.\nEkblomR, Wolf J B W. Evolutionary Applications, 2014, 7(9):1026-1042\n2.6 基因组比较\n•Pan-genomics in the human genome era \nSherman and Salzberg, 2020\n2.7 基因组数据库\nNCBIgenome browserUCSC genome browserENSEMBL genome browse\n10.7 基因组数据库\nhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/datasets/genome/\n10.7 基因组数据库\nhttps://genome.ucsc.edu/\n\n10.7 基因组数据库\nhttps://asia.ensembl.org/index.html\n\nReference•Blanchette, M. Computation and analysis of genomic multi-sequence alignments. Annual review of genomics and human genetics2007;8:193-2110.•Clarke, J., et al.Continuous base identification for single-molecule nanoporeDNA sequencing. Nature nanotechnology2009;4(4):265-270.•Conesa, A., et al.Blast2GO: a universal tool for annotation, visualization and analysis in functional genomics research. Bioinformatics 2005;21(18):3674-3676.•Earl, D., et al.Alignathon: a competitive assessment of whole-genome alignment methods. Genome research2014;24(12):2077-2089.•Ghurye, J. and Pop, M. Modern technologies and algorithms for scaffolding assembled genomes. PLoScomputational biology2019;15(6):e1006994.•Jones, P ., et al.InterProScan5: genome-scale protein function classification. Bioinformatics (Oxford, England)2014;30(9):1236-1240.•Jung, H., et al.Twelve quick steps for genome assembly and annotation in the classroom. PLoScomputational biology2020;16(11):e1008325.•Minkin, I. and Medvedev, P . Scalable multiple whole-genome alignment and locally collinear block construction with SibeliaZ. Nature communications2020;11(1):6327.•Mudge, J.M. and Harrow, J. The state of play in higher eukaryote gene annotation. Nature reviews. Genetics2016;17(12):758-772.•Pang E , Cao H , Zhang B , et al. Crop Genome Annotation: A Case Study for the Brassica rapaGenome[M]// The Brassica rapaGenome. Springer Berlin Heidelberg, 2015.•Paten, B., et al.Cactus graphs for genome comparisons. Journal of computational biology : a journal of computational molecular cell biology2011;18(3):469-481.\n\nReference•Putnam, N.H., et al.Chromosome-scale shotgun assembly using an in vitro method for long-range linkage. Genome research2016;26(3):342-350.•Ren, J., et al.Alignment-Free Sequence Analysis and Applications. Annual review of biomedical data science2018;1:93-114.•Rivals, I., et al.Enrichment or depletion of a GO category within a class of genes: which test? Bioinformatics (Oxford, England)2007;23(4):401-407.•Schadt, E.E., Turner, S. and Kasarskis, A. A window into third-generation sequencing. Human molecular genetics2010;19(R2):R227-240.•Sherman, R.M. and Salzberg, S.L. Pan-genomics in the human genome era. Nature reviews. Genetics2020;21(4):243-254.•Simpson, J.T. and Pop, M. The Theory and Practice of Genome Sequence Assembly. Annual review of genomics and human genetics2015;16:153-172.•Yandell, M. and Ence, D. A beginner\'s guide to eukaryotic genome annotation. Nature reviews. Genetics2012;13(5):329-342.\n\n','uploads/knowledge_bases/27/genomics.pdf','pdf','','2026-07-17 14:44:42','2026-07-17 14:44:42',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
